+# Isolated construction ownership evidence
+
+The original evidence checkout at `/home/sway/Code/sing-tun-ownership-evidence-sol-20260930`, commit `68b1913cceb196e9706f3dd8c4e863d32ffe0cae`, freezes the local cached source of `github.com/sagernet/sing-tun@v0.9.6-0.20260924073434-3077c705bbdb`. It is an evidence fixture, not a production dependency patch. The module cache and published source remain unchanged. This separate birth-ownership worktree now replaces the reproduction test with a fake-only regression; its real backends are Unsupported and it is forbidden for production integration. See `OWNERSHIP-SLICE1-CONTRACT.md` for that separate scope.
+
+The only production-code seam is a private function checked at entry to `startNFQueue`. The injected error occurs before any NFQueue, route or firewall acquire. The test supplies an executable fake `iptables`, whose `-S` response represents the rules of running instance A. Instance B uses the same table name, has no acquired rules, and exercises the pinned `Start` and `Close` implementations. Both an unstarted Close and the failed Start issue `-D`, `-F`, and `-X` commands against A's rules in nat, mangle and filter. No system iptables/nftables executable or kernel rule operation is used.
+
+Reproduce offline with the cached Go 1.25.5 toolchain:
+
+```sh
+cd /home/sway/Code/sing-tun-ownership-evidence-sol-20260930
+env GOWORK=off GOTOOLCHAIN=local GOPROXY=off GOSUMDB=off \
+  /home/sway/go/pkg/mod/golang.org/toolchain@v0.0.1-go1.25.5.linux-amd64/bin/go \
+  test -mod=mod -modfile=ownership-evidence.mod -race -count=1 \
+  -run TestOwnershipEvidence -v .
+```
+
+The alternate modfile and sum freeze already-resolved dependencies from the pinned sing-box build, with module identity changed to sing-tun and its self-require removed. This avoids fetching unused uncached dependencies from the original sing-tun module graph. It does not change production manifests or dependency resolution.
+
+The command trace proves that the pinned implementation attempts to remove another instance's same-name rules before B acquires any rule. It does not claim a live firewall integration test or a complete ownership audit. Dependency remediation requires a separate design review and per-acquire ownership evidence.
